# New model experiment

A model added under `models/<model>/` is not finished until it has passed these commands, in order, through `python -m src.pipeline.run`. Do not start `ablate` from the full column list. `ablate` only adds auxiliary columns that are missing from `models/<model>/best`.

1. `train --model <model> --features original` fits the ten `train.csv` columns and writes the first `best/` snapshot.
2. `ablate --model <model>` probes each auxiliary column. Ridge and the MLP call a column promising only when its search RMSE is at least 1% below that round's set A. XGBoost and CatBoost call it promising when the search RMSE is strictly lower. Those probes do not change `best/`. Set C, the current columns plus every promising column, replaces `best/` only when its own search RMSE is lower. Stop when a round has no promising column or set C does not win.
3. `finalize --model <model>` retrains the columns already in `best/` with that model's larger budget and writes `final/`. This stage does not add or drop columns. Search RMSE selects the stopped iterate.
4. `submit --model <model>` predicts `Data/test.csv` joined by row order to `Data/auxiliary_features/test_features.csv`. It writes `outputs/predictions/<model>_final.csv` from the `final/` weights and `outputs/predictions/<model>_refit.csv` after fitting every labeled month with the stopped size frozen.

Confirm RMSE is recorded and is not an acceptance signal. Do not paste metrics into `design.md`. The generated sections come from `docs/logs`. A capped `--max-rows` run is not evidence about the full training table.
